  "title": "Support checkPoolLiveAllocations with pluggable device",
  "issue_id": "163257",
  "bug_description": "### 🚀 The feature, motivation and pitch\n\n# Summary \n\nPytorch currently supports using separate device allocators via `torch.cuda.memory.change_memory_allocator`.  However, this breaks torch compile functionality:\n\n```\nRuntimeError: pluggable does not yet support checkPoolLiveAllocations. If you need it, please file an issue describing your use case.\n```\n\nI'd like to request pytorch support `checkPoolLiveAllocations` when using non-standard memory pool allocators.\n\n## Use Case\n\nI am doing performance optimizations for a neural operator network with a complicated preprocessing pipeline.  For optimal performance, and memory management, it's critical to share the memory pool between pytorch and rapids, via the rapids memory manager:\n\n```python\n    import rmm\n    from rmm.allocators.torch import rmm_torch_allocator\n    import torch\n\n    rmm.reinitialize(pool_allocator=True)\n    torch.cuda.memory.change_current_allocator(rmm_torch_allocator)\n```\n\nThe preprocessing pipeline needs to compute a kNN operation, and the `cuml` kNN is the most performant for this workload.\n\nOn the other hand, on H100 the model itself has relatively small kernels and gpu utilization is poor: the GPU is finishing nearly every kernel before the next one can launch.  This would straightforward to improve with cuda graphs and triton fusions via `torch.compile`, however, the changed memory allocator and end-to-end model compilation are incompatible.  The full traceback is here:\n\n```\n[rank0]:W0918 06:55:44.376000 537275 torch/_logging/_internal.py:1130] [0/0] Profiler function <class 'torch.autograd.profiler.record_function'> will be ignored\nError executing job with overrides: []\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/user_data/workdir/physicsnemo-domino-inference/examples/cfd/external_aerodynamics/domino/src/train.py\", line 548, in main\n    avg_loss = train_epoch(\n               ^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/user_data/workdir/physicsnemo-domino-inference/examples/cfd/external_aerodynamics/domino/src/train.py\", line 188, in train_epoch\n    prediction_vol, prediction_surf = model(sampled_batched)\n                                      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/torch/nn/modules/module.py\", line 1751, in _wrapped_call_impl\n    return self._call_impl(*args, **kwargs)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/torch/nn/modules/module.py\", line 1762, in _call_impl\n    return forward_call(*args, **kwargs)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/user_data/workdir/physicsnemo-domino-inference/physicsnemo/models/domino/model.py\", line 1910, in forward\n    encoding_g_vol = self.geo_rep_volume(geo_centers_vol, p_grid, sdf_grid)\n                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/torch/nn/modules/module.py\", line 1751, in _wrapped_call_impl\n    return self._call_impl(*args, **kwargs)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/torch/nn/modules/module.py\", line 1762, in _call_impl\n    return forward_call(*args, **kwargs)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/torch/_dynamo/eval_frame.py\", line 658, in _fn\n    return fn(*args, **kwargs)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/user_data/workdir/physicsnemo-domino-inference/physicsnemo/models/domino/model.py\", line 618, in forward\n    scaled_sdf = scale_sdf(sdf)\n                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/user_data/workdir/physicsnemo-domino-inference/physicsnemo/models/domino/model.py\", line 85, in scale_sdf\n    def scale_sdf(sdf: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/torch/_dynamo/eval_frame.py\", line 850, in _fn\n    return fn(*args, **kwargs)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/torch/_functorch/aot_autograd.py\", line 1207, in forward\n    return compiled_fn(full_args)\n           ^^^^",
